cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these formalizations, please cite this repository as below, and
  cite the original authors of each result, named in the README and in each
  module's docstring.
title: >-
  lean-classical-upstream: classical results in algorithmic information
  theory, learning theory, ergodic theory and realizability, machine-checked
  in Lean 4
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Palamarchuk
    given-names: Mykola
    email: lividgreen@gmail.com
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2106-5777
    affiliation: Independent researcher
repository-code: https://github.com/lividgreen/lean-classical-upstream
url: https://lividgreen.github.io/lean-classical-upstream/
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib package of classical results with their proofs, each
  labelled by its standing in Lean — formalized (first in Lean here), ported
  (proved elsewhere in a form that could not be used, so re-proved) or
  duplicated (proved elsewhere, a candidate for removal in favour of the
  original): Chaitin's incompleteness theorem for consistent first-order
  theories in its plain and additive forms; Levin's coding theorem on a
  universal prefix machine built from serialized codes; the statistical-query
  model with verified learners; Ville's inequality; Hoeffding's bound for
  finite-state Markov chains under a spectral gap; assemblies over Kleene's
  first algebra; finite Shannon information theory; and a port of the
  pointwise Birkhoff ergodic theorem. No sorry, no native_decide, standard
  axioms only, with each capstone's axiom footprint asserted by a
  build-enforced guard.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - algorithmic information theory
  - Kolmogorov complexity
  - Chaitin incompleteness
  - statistical queries
  - Ville's inequality
  - realizability
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23257423
# Deliberately only the concept DOI (decision 2026-07-28, as in the companion
# package): per-version DOIs are minted after the tag, so an in-repo list is
# always one behind; Zenodo's record lists every version, and the concept DOI
# resolves to the latest.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23257423
    description: >-
      Concept DOI — resolves to the latest archived version, and its Zenodo
      record lists the per-version DOIs.
